---
name: upgrade-sc-compose
version: 2.0.0
description: Unattended sc-compose upgrade - edit the repo pin, test it, PR, and release when nothing else is in flight.
format: toml
required_variables:
  - parent
  - ref
  - phase
  - from_version
  - to_version
  - priority
---
{#
sc-compose beads formula (sc-compose/beads/v1), attached with
`sc-compose bead attach` under the phase root of one upgrade run. Poured ids
are <parent>.<ref>-<step>.

The repo pin is the only thing this formula changes. Other skills and kits
declare their own minimum versions and are not edited here. The run needs no
input from Rand; every decision and escalation goes to omega-prime@hermes.
#}
formula = "upgrade-sc-compose"
description = "Upgrade sc-compose {{{ from_version }}} -> {{{ to_version }}} (phase-{{{ phase }}})."
version = 1
type = "workflow"

[[steps]]
id = "upgrade"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: pin sc-compose {{{ to_version }}}"
description = """
## Deliverables
1. `.claude/lib/sc_compose_dependency.py`: `SC_COMPOSE_PIN` and the `sc-compose==` install pin read {{{ to_version }}}. Minimum-version constants are not changed.
2. Read randlee/sc-compose at tag v{{{ to_version }}}: every `CHANGELOG.md` section after {{{ from_version }}} up to {{{ to_version }}}, `docs/migration-notes.md` and `docs/migration/`. List each breaking change, deprecation and recommended change in this bead's notes. For each one, `git grep` the repo for the affected command, flag, API or template syntax and either (a) apply the change to the repo-owned use in this layer, covered by deliverable 4 or 5, or (b) record "not used" with the grep. A use in a kit- or other-skill-owned file is not edited: file a GitHub issue against the owning repo and link it in the notes.
3. Two scratch environments, A = sc-compose {{{ from_version }}} and B = sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} (release CLI binary on PATH plus `pip install sc-compose==<v>` in a venv). In each, record `sc-compose --version` and the wheel's version; a run whose recorded versions do not match is void.
4. In A and in B, run the rendering suite and record pass/fail per test: `python3 -m pytest -q .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/tests .claude/skills/atm-beads/tests .claude/skills/triaging-findings/tests bindings/sc-lint-py/python/sc_lint/tests/test_orchestration_contracts.py`.
5. In A and in B, run `sc-compose bead validate` and `sc-compose bead preview-pour` (preview-attach for attach formulas) on every formula the team pours: `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/formulas/sprint-group.formula.toml.j2`, `finding-group.formula.toml.j2`, and this formula, with fixed sample variables. Diff B's JSON output against A's.
6. Verdict in this bead's notes: BREAKING when a test passing in A fails in B, or a formula's validate/preview output differs between A and B; the notes list each such test or formula with its output or diff. A test failing in both is pre-existing and reported, not breaking. NOT BREAKING otherwise.
7. With B installed, `just lint` and `just test` pass.
8. `git grep -n "sc-compose==\\|SC_COMPOSE_PIN"` finds no repo-owned pin other than deliverable 1; any new one is listed in the notes and added to this formula's deliverable 1.
"""
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:dev"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "dev"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
difficulty = "fast"
branch = "sprint/{{{ phase }}}-1-sc-compose-{{{ to_version }}}"
pr_target = "integrate/phase-{{{ phase }}}"
owned_paths = [".claude/lib/sc_compose_dependency.py", "repo-owned files changed by deliverable 2"]

[[steps]]
id = "qa"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: QA sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} pin"
description = """
## Deliverables
1. quality-mgr checks the upgrade bead's changelog list against the sc-compose CHANGELOG and migration docs (each item applied, not used, or issued), re-runs deliverables 3-6 independently at the layer's pushed head and confirms the recorded versions, per-test results, formula diffs and BREAKING verdict match; only the pin and the deliverable 2 changes are in the diff; CI on the layer is green or its failure is a recorded breaking change.
"""
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:qa"]
needs = ["upgrade"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "qa"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
difficulty = "normal"
checked_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-upgrade"

[[steps]]
id = "pr_develop"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: PR to develop"
description = """
Decision point 1 (breaking or not). Land the layer on integrate/phase-{{{ phase }}} (`gh stack merge <stack> --yes --merge`), open the ready integrate/phase-{{{ phase }}} -> develop PR, and request review from `rand-lee` (`gh api -X POST repos/randlee/sc-lint/pulls/<n>/requested_reviewers -f 'reviewers[]=rand-lee'`). Never merge it; only Rand merges to develop.
- Breaking (upgrade notes record a failure): put the failing tests and output in the PR description, run `atm send omega-prime@hermes "sc-lint: sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} upgrade is BREAKING. Rand, please review <PR link>. <failing tests>"`, close release as not planned, and close this bead.
- Not breaking, CI green: run `atm send omega-prime@hermes "sc-lint: sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} upgrade, CI green. Rand, please complete <PR link>."` and close this bead.
"""
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:land"]
needs = ["qa"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "lead"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"

[[steps]]
id = "release"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: patch release PR to main"
description = """
Decision point 2, after Rand merges the PR to develop. Other work in progress = an open phase or release bead, or another open PR to develop.
- Other work in progress: run `atm send omega-prime@hermes "sc-lint: sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} on develop; release deferred because <work>."` and close this bead.
- Otherwise: the publisher bumps the patch version on release/<next-patch>-prep (PR to develop, `rand-lee` reviewer, omega-prime notified when green), then after Rand merges it runs publish-preflight to GO, tags the release candidate, and opens the develop -> main PR with `rand-lee` as reviewer. When CI is green run `atm send omega-prime@hermes "sc-lint: <version> release PR to main, preflight GO, CI green. Rand, please complete <PR link>."`. If preflight or CI cannot go green, run `atm send omega-prime@hermes "sc-lint: <version> release blocked: <cause>. <link>"` and leave this bead open. No agent merges to develop or main.
"""
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:release"]
needs = ["pr_develop"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "publisher"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
